I'm like coming home.

00:09:35.125 --> 00:09:37.270
- You're like, so wonderful.
- And quickly, side note,

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:39.320
that was the day that I got Brad Pitt.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:42.490
Y'all, I'm walking on the red
carpet, I bump into Brad Pitt.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.540
I panic and I say to him,
"Hey Brad, Kit Pitt".

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.430
And like I'm not Kit Pit.

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:49.370
And he says, "Maiden or married?"

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.350
And I was like oh my
god, he's talking back!

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:52.877
I said maiden, and he goes,

00:09:52.877 --> 00:09:54.290
"There's not many of us in there",

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:55.300
and he starts talking to me.

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:56.982
Then I say, "I love architecture."

00:09:56.982 --> 00:09:58.760
(women talk over one another)

00:09:58.760 --> 00:09:59.740
And then they pull him away.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.200
But anyway, so I had a Pitt moment.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.410
- I love your random things!

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.640
Kit Pitt and I love architecture.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.150
- Exactly, 'cause apparently I read

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:08.470
in an article that he likes architecture.

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:11.930
It went south quickly, but I
get home and I'm feeling myself

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:14.047
and I'm in my dress and literally
the whole family's like,

00:10:14.047 --> 00:10:15.160
"Mom, what's for dinner?

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:16.840
Are you gonna make your parma rosa?"

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.630
And like, I couldn't
have loved it any more,

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:19.860
like nobody really cares

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:20.740
about my day job.
- I love that.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:22.280
- Yeah.
- My kids look at me

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.520
'cause I don't wear hair and makeup

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:24.490
- Ever.
- if I'm not working.

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.430
- Yes.
- I have to be paid

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:26.383
to do this.
- Yes.

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:30.850
- 'Cause I'm allergic as well,
so it stings, the eye makeup.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:32.230
I love you, Glo!

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.820
But I love my makeup artist, though,

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.430
but I, when I get home, my
son, especially he freaks out.

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:39.390
He's like, "Can you take a shower?"

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:41.037
'Cause it freaks him
out, 'cause he's like,

00:10:41.037 --> 00:10:42.410
"I don't like you in that."

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.780
He was like, I like you,
and I'm, that's so nice.

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:46.380
- I know, my kids are like that.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:47.670
My husband's the opposite.

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.460
'Cause on the weekend I'm
baseball hat, no makeup.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.830
He was like, "Where's that Monday through

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:53.960
Friday lady?"
- This is false advertisement.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:54.793
- Yeah, exactly!

00:10:54.793 --> 00:10:56.680
Could that lady with the
lashes ever come home,

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:57.873
and I'm like beat with my hat on.

00:10:57.873 --> 00:11:00.197
- And you're like, no,
you're lucky (laughs).

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:02.820
So wait, what do you love most

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:04.050
about doing "Access" these days?

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:04.980
'Cause you've been doing it for a bit.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:05.850
- For a bit.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.340
I think we've started
interviewing a lot of

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:11.630
normal people; by normal,
I mean not celebrities

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:12.990
- Yeah.
- with extraordinary stories

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:15.100
and I find myself so moved by them.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:16.440
- Yeah.
- I don't know if it's my age

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.140
or where I am now, but
there are so many times

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:19.980
that I'm blown away by the human strength,

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.710
and that's why I like the
Olympics and everything

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:23.460
watching that story, the human spirit.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:24.760
- Yeah.
- So those are the stories

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:25.618
that are moving me but I'm

00:11:25.618 --> 00:11:26.451
just having a ball.
- I think we need

00:11:26.451 --> 00:11:28.253
them more now too,
that's why I like it too.

00:11:28.253 --> 00:11:30.010
- Don't you?
- This show came at such

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:33.330
a perfect time for me and my
crew because it's like, yeah,

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.500
I like interviewing the celebrities,

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.880
I like doing it, but it's really cool.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.150
You get to highlight these
people doing amazing things

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:41.250
and then you get to see the
positive side of humanity,

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:43.060
'cause it can get real dark, real quick.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:44.880
- You're doing one today, I
was listening to the team.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:45.900
What are we doing in Vegas?

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:48.030
Like I heard that and that's
what moves me these days.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.180
- I know, it's incredible.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.850
People are actually thinking
of others, it's awesome.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.268
- Yeah, how about that thing?

00:11:52.268 --> 00:11:54.330
- It's a good idea.
- Yeah, it's a good idea.

